# Type Codes are used so that the server can tell the client a destination
# directory (configured on client), for example the type code "T" could be set
# for the label sonarr, so the payload is transferred to the TV directory.

# Codes are 5 fields (space separated, NO quoting):
#   TORRENT_FIELD   CONDITIONAL   COMPARISON_VALUE   TYPE_CODE   [ALREADY_CODED]
#
#   TORRENT_FIELD    torrent value index: KEY | HASH | LABEL | TRACKER | PATH
#   CONDITIONAL      comparison applied: IS | CONTAINS | NOT
#   COMPARISON_VALUE what the field is compared to (do NOT quote it)
#   TYPE_CODE        code applied if the comparison succeeds
#   ALREADY_CODED    tier 2: the rule only applies if the current code already
#                    equals this value. Leave the 5th column EMPTY for tier 1
#                    (do NOT write "" - the parser compares literally).
#
# Order Matters, Tier 1 first, Tier 2 after.

# Examples:

# LABEL IS sonarr T
# If the current torrent LABEL is (IS) sonarr, the type code is T
# provided the type code hasn't been set yet.

# TRACKER CONTAINS hatc A
# If the TRACKER contains the string hatc (ie http://tracker.whatcd.net/announce.php)
# then the type code is set to A (audio/music).

# KEY CONTAINS eopardy J T
# If the KEY (torrent name) contains the string eopardy (ie Jeopardy.2022.09.13.720p)
# and the type code is already T (TV), the type code is set to J.

# KEY CONTAINS 2024 N M
# If the KEY (torrent name) contains the string 2024 and the type code is already
# M (Movie), then the code is set to N for New Movie.

LABEL IS sonarr T
TRACKER CONTAINS hatc A
TRACKER CONTAINS tackove B
TRACKER CONTAINS emp V
TRACKER CONTAINS ageddon B
KEY CONTAINS eopardy J T
KEY CONTAINS 2024 N M
